a 15.000 euros, justo por debajo del límite legal. Si esos importes se repartieran como en la franja inmediatamente inferior, lo esperable serían 29,8 contratos. La razón entre observados y esperados es 2,8, con un intervalo de confianza del 95 % de 2,1 a 3,6. En diciembre se adjudicó el 11 % de los contratos junto al límite, mientras que diciembre supone el 8 % de todos sus contratos de servicios y suministros. Los contratos junto al límite se reparten entre 62 adjudicatarios distintos. El contrato [1], de 14.535 euros, se adjudicó en diciembre de 2025.\nQué no pueden demostrar: El hecho de que se adjudiquen contratos al límite no indica que haya sido un error. Puede deberse a razones legítimas, como necesidades específicas o precios de mercado.\nQué se puede revisar: Comprobar si los contratos [1] y [2] atienden la misma necesidad. Verificar si el adjudicatario A repite contratos en distintas áreas. Analizar si los contratos de diciembre están relacionados con un mismo proyecto.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 82 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 29.8 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 2.8, with a 95% confidence interval of 2.1 to 3.6. December accounts for 11% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 8% of all its services and supplies contracts. The contracts just under the limit are spread across 62 different awardees. Contract [1], for 14,535 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts in December does not indicate improper activity. Similar patterns can occur naturally due to seasonal demand or budget cycles. The number of contracts near the limit does not prove wrongdoing, as market prices or budget constraints may influence decisions.\nWhat can be checked: Check the dates and values of December contracts to see if they align with typical patterns. Review the awardees' contracts to identify if multiple contracts serve the same purpose. Look for repeated purchases from the same provider to assess if they meet distinct needs or if they are part of a larger procurement strategy.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["fo5Nq1fjgZY%2FbjW6njtWLw%3D%3D","UoXoOZSbhaN%2FP7lJ7Fu0SA%3D%3D","NXHGYyM%2FH1j%2B3JAijKO%2Bkg%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-16"}}